Illegal immigration-identify, report, detain 25LSO-0387, 1.1
and deport.
Corrected Copy
FISCAL NOTE
The fiscal impact to the Department of Workforce Services (Department) is an
expenditure increase of an estimated $772.00. This bill requires the Department
to verify citizenship status through the Systematic Alien Verification of
Entitlement program (SAVE) operated by the United States Department of Homeland
Security. A fee is associated with every verification conducted. The Department
has calculated the estimated expenditures based on a fee of $1.50 per
verification on an estimated 101 verifications for months July through September
2025 and $2.00 per verification for months October through June 2026. The
Department assumes that 3% of all applicants in the qualified programs will need
to be verified for citizenship status and eligible for benefits through SAVE.
The fiscal impact to the judicial system is indeterminable due to an unknown
number of cases.
The expenditure increase to the Department of Administration & Information is
indeterminable.
There is no significant fiscal or personnel impact to the Attorney General’s
Office (Office). However, this bill could create an increased workload to the
Office.
No significant fiscal or personnel impact to the Department of Health, Department
of Family Services, Department of Corrections, and the Wyoming Department of
Transportation.
